                        "entry_id": "e353ddff-a87a-3c9d-ba21-8eb3ee1cd065",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not seeking to produce a profit (a financial gain)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f5b677e-c1de-43bd-8bf5-a4c41ac38e05",
                                "sense_id": "9d815d9a-7bf1-3d59-a952-67c7ef3774bd",
                                "text": "Here in New York, plush rehabilitation centers literally canvass for big-paying clients whose insurance will cover the average $11,000 to $14,000 cost for a month's treatment. Meanwhile, there are only 12,000 non-profit treatment beds in the state for a conservatively estimated 350,000 addicts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "63f30d47-7463-4d20-b906-ef34bae3533d",
                                "sense_id": "9d815d9a-7bf1-3d59-a952-67c7ef3774bd",
                                "text": "The site's infrastructure (but not its content) is now run by the nonprofit Wikimedia Foundation (WMF), which will be described in depth in Chapter 17."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
